Task: Fix the iOS Status Bar correctly in BOTH Dark Mode and Light Mode.

There is currently a problem with the native iPhone status bar at the very top of the app.

The time, network/Wi-Fi signal, cellular indicator, and battery icon are not always readable because the status bar foreground color is not synchronized correctly with the app theme.

I want this fixed at the native iOS level.

====================================================
CURRENT PROBLEM
====================================================

In Dark Mode:
- The app background is black.
- The status bar icons/text can become dark or disappear against the black background.
- Time, signal, Wi-Fi/5G and battery must remain clearly visible.

In Light Mode:
- The app background is light.
- The status bar icons/text must become dark so they remain readable.

The status bar must NEVER have the wrong foreground style for the current theme.

====================================================
EXPECTED BEHAVIOR
====================================================

DARK MODE:
- Status bar background visually blends with the dark app background.
- Time = white/light.
- Network/Wi-Fi/cellular icons = white/light.
- Battery = white/light.

LIGHT MODE:
- Status bar background visually blends with the light app background.
- Time = black/dark.
- Network/Wi-Fi/cellular icons = black/dark.
- Battery = black/dark.

====================================================
IMPORTANT
====================================================

Do NOT fake the status bar inside React.

Do NOT draw custom time/battery icons.

Use the real native iOS StatusBar behavior.

The actual iOS system status bar must update when:
- the app launches,
- the user changes theme,
- the user navigates between screens,
- the app returns from background.

====================================================
IMPLEMENTATION
====================================================

Audit the current iOS/Capacitor status bar implementation first.

Check for:
- StatusBar plugin configuration
- preferredStatusBarStyle
- UIViewControllerBasedStatusBarAppearance
- native Swift overrides
- Capacitor status bar calls
- theme listeners
- conflicting old code

There must be ONE source of truth for the status bar style.

Dark theme:
use light status bar content.

Light theme:
use dark status bar content.

If old React/Swift/Capacitor code conflicts with this behavior, remove or consolidate it instead of stacking another workaround.

====================================================
